.TH tkutical n 0.4 tkutils
.SH "tkutils::tkutical  (optional widget)"
.PP
Month calendar widget that wraps the \fBtical\fR library. OPTIONAL: not in the tkutils umbrella; require it directly once \fBtical\fR is on the module path (\fBtical::view::month\fR + \fBtical::render::canvas\fR).
.SS API
.CS
set w [::tkutils::tkutical::widget .w ?-year Y? ?-month M? \
        ?-weeknumbers 0|1? ?-fontsize N? ?-holidays REGION? \
        ?-selectmode none|single|multiple? ?-command CMD? ?-events LIST?]
::tkutils::tkutical::setMonth   $w year month     ;# -> {y m}; throws on bad month
::tkutils::tkutical::getMonth   $w                ;# -> {y m}
::tkutils::tkutical::next       $w
::tkutils::tkutical::prev       $w
::tkutils::tkutical::today      $w
::tkutils::tkutical::refresh    $w
::tkutils::tkutical::selectMode $w none|single|multiple
::tkutils::tkutical::getSelection   $w            ;# -> sorted ISO dates
::tkutils::tkutical::setSelection   $w {dates / A..B ranges}
::tkutils::tkutical::clearSelection $w
::tkutils::tkutical::canvasWidget   $w            ;# underlying canvas
::tkutils::tkutical::setView    $w month|week     ;# switch view; throws on bad view
::tkutils::tkutical::getView    $w                ;# -> month|week
::tkutils::tkutical::setDate    $w iso            ;# set the focused date (YYYY-MM-DD)
::tkutils::tkutical::getDate    $w                ;# -> focused ISO date
::tkutils::tkutical::setEvents  $w LIST           ;# appointments; redraws
::tkutils::tkutical::getEvents  $w
.CE
.PP
\fB\-command CMD\fR is called as \fBCMD $w $selection\fR on selection changes (selection modes only). Default \fB\-selectmode single\fR. Errorcodes: \fB{TKUTILS TKUTICAL MONTH}\fR, \fB{TKUTILS TKUTICAL SELECTMODE}\fR, \fB{TKUTILS TKUTICAL VIEW}\fR, \fB{TKUTILS TKUTICAL DATE}\fR, \fB{TKUTILS TKUTICAL EVENTS}\fR.
.PP
\fB\-events LIST\fR / \fBsetEvents\fR (since 0.4): appointments in the format of \fBtical::event\fR (\fBsummary\fR, \fBdtstart\fR, \fBdtend\fR, \fBrrule\fR ...). The views put them in the cells, a series on each of its days; the canvas draws dots in the month and titles in the week. They stay across navigation and view changes. Needs tical 1.1 or later; with tical 1.0.x a non\-empty list is an error \fB{TKUTILS TKUTICAL EVENTS}\fR.
.CS
::tkutils::tkutical::widget .cal -events {
    {summary Zahnarzt dtstart 2025-10-14T09:00 dtend 2025-10-14T10:00}
    {summary Sport dtstart 2025-10-07T18:00 rrule {freq WEEKLY byday {TU TH}}}
}
.CE
.SS "Install / run"
.IP \(bu
Drop \fBlib/tm/tkutils/tkutical\-0.1.tm\fR into the tkutils tree (do NOT add it to the umbrella \-\- it is optional, like tkutablelist/tkusqlite).
.IP \(bu
Add the optional\-widgets row already prepared in README.md.
.IP \(bu
Launcher: \fBbin/tkutical.tcl\fR (set \fBTICAL_DIR=/path/to/tical\fR or keep tical as a sibling repo). e.g.  \fBTICAL_DIR=.../tical wish bin/tkutical.tcl 2025 10\fR
.SS Verification
.IP \(bu
tkutical.test: 17/17 on Tcl/Tk 8.6 and 9.0 (Xvfb), tical 1.1.1.
.IP \(bu
With tical (or Tk) absent the suite SKIPS via the \fBtical\fR constraint (all skipped, 0 failed) \-\- never breaks the tkutils runner, which already runs each test in its own process.
